    "result_text": "The AcceptanceTest is the only test class in the suite, and it passes; the full `test` phase is BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that on a successful owner create, a welcome notification be enqueued by emitting a line via the `NOTIFY` logger containing the owner id and the memberId.\n\nI kept structural impact minimal:\n\n- **New cohesive unit** \u2014 `service/WelcomeNotification.java`: a tiny final class with its own `NOTIFY` logger and a single `enqueue(Owner)` method that logs `welcome owner id={} memberId={}`. Zero surrounding complexity (WMC_other = 0), CC = 1.\n- **One-line hook** \u2014 added `WelcomeNotification.enqueue(owner)` to the existing post-save side-effect method `OwnerCreatedEvent.emit(...)`. This runs after `saveOwner`, so the owner id is already assigned (unlike `enrich`, which runs pre-save). `OwnerCreatedEvent` is a small class (WMC_other = 1, CC of `emit` = 1, one changed line).\n\nCrucially, the large `OwnerRestControllerV1` class was left untouched, avoiding its high WMC_other cost. Two files touched, both with trivial per-function cost.\n\nThe `NOTIFY` line is confirmed in the run: `INFO NOTIFY - welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2700C7EBD71`. The acceptance test and full suite are green (BUILD SUCCESS).",
